Supreme People's Court

Notice on Issuing the Opinions on Certain Issues Concerning Case Filing and Case Closure of Enforcement Cases

Fa Fa [2014] No. 26

To the High People's Courts of all provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government; the Military Court of the People's Liberation Army; the Production and Construction Corps Branch of the High People's Court of Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region:

To unify the standards for filing and closing enforcement cases and to regulate enforcement actions, the Supreme People's Court has formulated the "Opinions on Certain Issues Concerning Case Filing and Case Closure of Enforcement Cases," which are hereby issued. Please implement them accordingly, and strengthen the management of the filing and closure of enforcement cases by establishing and improving a unified, practical, fully functional, scientific, and effective case management system for the three levels of courts within your jurisdiction. These Opinions shall come into force on January 1, 2015. The enforcement division shall promptly communicate with the case filing division to ensure a smooth transition between the old and new years regarding the filing and closure of enforcement cases, and to ensure the full implementation of the filing and closure standards stipulated in these Opinions.

December 17, 2014

Opinions on Certain Issues Concerning Case Filing and Case Closure of Enforcement Cases

To unify the standards for filing and closing enforcement cases and to regulate enforcement actions, these Opinions are formulated in accordance with the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China and other laws and judicial interpretations, taking into account the actual circumstances of the people's courts' enforcement work.

Article 1 For the purposes of these Opinions, enforcement cases include enforcement implementation cases and enforcement review cases.

Enforcement implementation cases refer to cases where the people's court, upon application by the enforcement applicant, transfer by the judicial organ, entrustment, elevation, designation, or ex officio, enforces matters determined in legal documents that have taken legal effect and contain contents subject to compulsory enforcement.

Enforcement review cases refer to cases during the enforcement process where the people's court reviews and handles enforcement objections, appeals, petitions, requests for instructions, coordination, and decisions on the transfer of enforcement jurisdiction.

Article 2 Enforcement cases shall be uniformly reviewed and filed by the case filing organ of the people's court. If a people's tribunal is authorized to enforce cases it has adjudicated, it may conduct case filing review on its own. If laws or judicial interpretations allow for transfer for enforcement, the relevant judicial organ may transfer the case to the case filing organ for handling registration procedures.

After filing the case, the case filing organ shall issue a notice of acceptance of the enforcement case to the applicant in accordance with the provisions of laws and judicial interpretations.

Article 3 The people's court shall file enforcement cases that meet the filing standards stipulated by laws and judicial interpretations, and shall incorporate them into the unified management system for adjudication and enforcement cases.

The people's court shall not have enforcement cases outside the unified management system for adjudication and enforcement cases.

No case shall enter enforcement proceedings without being filed for any reason.

Article 4 When reviewing and filing cases, the case filing organ shall determine the type code and case number for enforcement cases in accordance with these Opinions, and shall not create type codes for cases in violation of these Opinions.

Article 5 The type code for enforcement implementation cases is "Zhi Zi (执字)", and the case number shall be determined in chronological order of filing, with separate sequencing. However, for cases enforcing property preservation rulings, the type code is "Zhi Bao Zi (执保字)", with the case number determined in chronological order of filing, with separate sequencing. For cases of resumed enforcement, the type code is "Zhi Hui Zi (执恢字)", with the case number determined in chronological order of filing, with separate sequencing.

Article 6 The people's court shall file the following cases as resumed enforcement cases:

(1) Where the enforcement applicant enters into a settlement agreement with the enforcement respondent due to fraud or coercion, and applies for resumption of enforcement of the original effective legal document;
(2) Where one party fails to perform or does not fully perform an enforcement settlement agreement, and the other party applies for resumption of enforcement of the original effective legal document;
(3) Where an enforcement implementation case is closed by a ruling to conclude the current enforcement proceedings, and thereafter it is discovered that the enforcement respondent has property available for enforcement, and the enforcement applicant applies or the people's court ex officio resumes enforcement;
(4) Where an enforcement implementation case is closed due to entrusted enforcement, but the entrustment is subsequently returned by the entrusted court that has already filed the case because the entrustment was improper;
(5) Where an enforcement case is terminated in accordance with the provisions of Article 257 of the Civil Procedure Law, and when the conditions for the enforcement applicant's application are met, the enforcement applicant applies for resumption of enforcement.

Article 7 Except for the following circumstances, the people's court shall not artificially split enforcement implementation cases:

(1) Where the payment content determined by the effective legal document is to be performed in installments, and upon the maturity of each installment, if the enforcement respondent fails to perform automatically, the enforcement applicant may apply for enforcement by installments, or may apply for enforcement of several or all matured claims together;
(2) Where the effective legal document determines that multiple debtors are each independently liable for specific debts, the enforcement applicant may apply for enforcement against each debtor separately, or may apply for enforcement against several or all debtors together;
(3) Where the effective legal document determines that multiple creditors each have specific claims (including claims by shares), each creditor may apply for enforcement separately;
(4) In cases concerning applications for enforcement of alimony, spousal support, or child support, involving monetary payment, the people's court shall review and file the case based on the amount of claims that have accrued at the time of application; claims that accrue during the enforcement process shall be subject to a separate application for enforcement. In cases involving personal rights, the people's court shall review and file the case based on the fact that the obligor has not performed its obligations at the time of application; if the obligor continues its passive conduct during the enforcement process, enforcement shall be carried out collectively based on the application of the enforcement applicant.

Article 8 For enforcement review cases, the type code and case number shall be determined according to the following rules:

(1) The type code for enforcement objection cases is "Zhi Yi Zi (执异字)", and the case number shall be determined in chronological order of filing, with separate sequencing;
(2) The type code for enforcement appeal cases is "Zhi Fu Zi (执复字)", and the case number shall be determined in chronological order of filing, with separate sequencing;
(3) The type code for enforcement supervision cases is "Zhi Jian Zi (执监字)", and the case number shall be determined in chronological order of filing, with separate sequencing;
(4) The type code for enforcement request for instructions cases is "Zhi Qing Zi (执请字)", and the case number shall be determined in chronological order of filing, with separate sequencing;
(5) The type code for enforcement coordination cases is "Zhi Xie Zi (执协字)", and the case number shall be determined in chronological order of filing, with separate sequencing.

Article 9 The people's court shall file the following cases as enforcement objection cases:

(1) Where a party or an interested person believes that the enforcement act of the people's court violates the law and raises a written objection;
(2) During the enforcement process, a person other than the party raises a written objection to the subject matter of enforcement;
(3) After the people's court accepts the enforcement application, a party raises an objection to jurisdiction;
(4) Where the enforcement applicant applies for the addition or change of the enforcement respondent;
(5) Where the enforcement respondent raises an objection to enforcement based on substantive grounds such as extinguishment of the claim, expiration of the time limit for applying for enforcement, or other grounds preventing enforcement;
(6) Where the enforcement respondent applies for non-enforcement of an arbitral award or a notarized creditor's document with compulsory enforcement effect granted by a notary public;
(7) Other cases where an enforcement objection may be filed in accordance with the law.

Article 10 The people's court shall file the following cases as enforcement appeal cases:

(1) Where a party or an interested person, dissatisfied with the ruling made by the people's court concerning items (1), (3), or (5) of Article 9 of these Opinions, applies to the next higher people's court for reconsideration;
(2) Except for additions arising from marital joint debts, failure of investors to contribute capital in accordance with the law, transfer of equity, and addition of a shareholder of a one-person company, where a party or an interested person, dissatisfied with the ruling made by the people's court concerning item (4) of Article 9 of these Opinions, applies to the next higher people's court for reconsideration;
(3) Where a party, dissatisfied with the ruling made by the people's court concerning item (6) of Article 9 of these Opinions regarding non-enforcement of a notarized creditor's document, rejection of an application for non-enforcement of a notarized creditor's document, non-enforcement of an arbitral award, or rejection of an application for non-enforcement of an arbitral award, applies to the next higher people's court for reconsideration;
(4) Other cases where reconsideration may be applied for in accordance with the law.

Article 11 Cases in which a higher people's court supervises a lower people's court, or the Supreme People's Court supervises local people's courts at all levels, shall be filed as enforcement supervision cases.

Article 12 The people's court shall file the following cases as enforcement request for instructions cases:

(1) Where a party applies to the people's court for enforcement of an arbitral award involving Hong Kong or Macao made by an arbitral institution on the mainland, or an arbitral award made by an arbitral institution of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region or the Macao Special Administrative Region, or an arbitral award made by an ad hoc arbitral tribunal in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region or the Macao Special Administrative Region, and upon review, the people's court considers that there are grounds for non-enforcement under the law, and before making a ruling, refers the matter to the higher people's court to which it is subordinate for review; and where the higher people's court agrees not to enforce, it refers the matter to the Supreme People's Court;
(2) Where a lower people's court requests instructions from a higher people's court in accordance with the law.

Article 13 The people's court shall file the following cases as enforcement coordination cases:

(1) Where different courts have disputes over the subject matter of enforcement between enforcement proceedings, or between enforcement and bankruptcy, compulsory liquidation, adjudication, or other proceedings, and after attempts at self-coordination fail to reach a consensus, they refer the matter to the common higher people's court for coordination;
(2) Where there is a dispute over enforcement between a court and public security or procuratorial authorities across the jurisdiction of different high people's courts, the enforcement court refers the matter to the high people's court to which it is subordinate for coordination with the high people's court where the relevant public security or procuratorial authority is located, to consult with the relevant authorities for resolution, or refers the matter to the Supreme People's Court for coordination;
(3) Where a party applies to different people's courts respectively for revocation and enforcement of an arbitral award involving Hong Kong or Macao made by an arbitral institution on the mainland, and the court that accepted the enforcement application has objections to the ruling made by the court that accepted the revocation application to revoke or not revoke the award, and cannot directly make an enforcement or non-enforcement ruling that conflicts with that ruling, it refers the matter to the common higher people's court for resolution;
(4) Where a party applies to a people's court for enforcement of an arbitral award involving Hong Kong or Macao made by an arbitral institution on the mainland, and after the people's court has made a ruling that enforcement shall be granted, one party applies to a people's court for revocation of the award; if the court that accepted the revocation application considers that the award should be revoked, and that court is not the same court that accepted the enforcement application, it refers the matter to the common higher people's court for resolution;
(5) Where an enforcement dispute crosses provinces, autonomous regions, or municipalities directly under the Central Government, it is referred to the Supreme People's Court for coordination;
(6) Other cases that shall be reported for coordination in accordance with the law.

Article 14 Except for cases enforcing property preservation rulings and cases of resumed enforcement, the methods of closing enforcement implementation cases include:

(1) Enforcement completed;
(2) Conclude the current enforcement proceedings;
(3) Termination of enforcement;
(4) Case closure;
(5) Non-enforcement;
(6) Dismissal of application.

Article 15 Where the enforcement content determined by the effective legal document has been fully completed through automatic performance by the enforcement respondent or compulsory enforcement by the people's court, or where the parties have reached an enforcement settlement agreement and the enforcement settlement agreement has been fully performed, the case may be closed by the method of "enforcement completed."

A notice of case closure shall be issued upon the completion of enforcement and served on the parties. If both parties acknowledge in writing that enforcement has been completed, or orally acknowledge and it is recorded in the record, there is no need to issue a notice of case closure.

The enforcement settlement agreement shall be attached to the case file. If no written enforcement settlement agreement is signed, the content of the oral settlement agreement shall be recorded in a record, which shall be attached to the file after being signed by the parties.

Article 16 Under any of the following circumstances, the case may be closed by the method of "conclude the current enforcement proceedings":

(1) The enforcement respondent indeed has no property available for enforcement, and the enforcement applicant agrees in writing to the conclusion of the current enforcement proceedings by the people's court;
(2) Suspension of enforcement due to the enforcement respondent having no property has lasted for two years, and upon verification, it is confirmed that the enforcement respondent indeed has no property available for enforcement;
(3) The enforcement applicant explicitly states that it cannot provide property or leads to property of the enforcement respondent, and after the people's court exhausts property investigation measures, the enforcement applicant acknowledges in writing that the people's court has determined that the enforcement respondent has no property available for enforcement;
(4) The property of the enforcement respondent cannot be auctioned or sold, or after two auctions for movable property or three auctions for immovable property or other property rights, the auction has failed, and the enforcement applicant refuses to accept or cannot be legally delivered the property in lieu of debt, and after the people's court exhausts property investigation measures, the enforcement respondent indeed has no other property available for enforcement;
(5) After the people's court exhausts property investigation measures, the enforcement respondent indeed has no property available for enforcement or has property but it is not suitable for compulsory enforcement, and the parties have reached a settlement agreement for installment performance, which has not been fully performed;
(6) The enforcement respondent indeed has no property available for enforcement, the enforcement applicant belongs to a particularly disadvantaged group, and the enforcement court has provided appropriate relief.

The people's court shall form a collegiate panel in accordance with the law to deliberate on whether to conclude the current enforcement proceedings.

A ruling to conclude the current enforcement proceedings shall be made and served on the enforcement applicant. The ruling shall specify the circumstances of the enforcement, the status of the enforcement applicant's claims that have been satisfied and not satisfied, the reasons for concluding the current enforcement proceedings, and the fact that if the enforcement respondent is discovered to have property available for enforcement, an application for resumption of enforcement may be filed.

Before ruling to conclude the current enforcement proceedings based on items (2), (4), (5), or (6) of the first paragraph of this Article, the enforcement applicant shall be informed that it may raise an objection within a specified period. If the enforcement applicant raises an objection, a separate collegiate panel shall be formed to hold a hearing with the parties on whether the enforcement respondent has property available for enforcement; if the enforcement applicant provides leads to property of the enforcement respondent, the people's court shall re-investigate and verify those leads; if it is discovered that the enforcement respondent has property available for enforcement, enforcement shall continue; if after the hearing it is determined that the enforcement respondent indeed has no property available for enforcement, and the enforcement applicant cannot provide property available for enforcement by the enforcement respondent, a ruling may be made to conclude the current enforcement proceedings.

The "people's court exhausts property investigation measures" mentioned in items (3), (4), and (5) of the first paragraph of this Article means that at least the following investigation items have been completed:

(1) If the enforcement respondent is a legal person or other organization, it shall inquire with banking financial institutions about bank deposits, with relevant real estate management departments about real estate registration, with corporate registration authorities about equity, and with relevant vehicle management authorities about vehicles, etc.;
(2) If the enforcement respondent is a natural person, it shall investigate and ascertain the property status or leads to property of the enforcement respondent from the enforcement respondent's employer and the surrounding community, including the source of economic income of the enforcement respondent, mature claims of the enforcement respondent, etc. If, based on leads to property, it is determined that the enforcement respondent has relatively high income, investigation shall be conducted in accordance with the investigation channels for legal persons or other organizations;
(3) Investigation items that can be completed through the Supreme People's Court's national court network enforcement inquiry and control system and the "point-to-point" network enforcement inquiry and control system of the high people's court to which the enforcement court is subordinate;
(4) Investigation items that must be completed as stipulated by laws and judicial interpretations.

After the people's court rules to conclude the current enforcement proceedings, if it is discovered that the enforcement respondent has property, enforcement may be resumed upon the application of the enforcement applicant or ex officio by the people's court. If the enforcement applicant applies for resumption of enforcement, it shall not be subject to the time limit for applying for enforcement.

Article 17 Under any of the following circumstances, the case may be closed by the method of "termination of enforcement":

(1) The applicant withdraws the application, or both parties reach an enforcement settlement agreement and the enforcement applicant withdraws the enforcement application;
(2) The legal document on which the enforcement is based is revoked;
(3) The enforcement respondent, being a citizen, dies, leaving no estate available for enforcement and no one liable for obligations;
(4) The right holder in a case seeking alimony, spousal support, or child support dies;
(5) The enforcement respondent, being a citizen, is unable to repay the debt due to financial hardship, has no source of income, and has lost the ability to work;
(6) The enforcement respondent, being an enterprise legal person or other organization, is dissolved, deregistered, has its business license revoked, or ceases operations or terminates, and has no property available for enforcement, no person to assume obligations, and no subject of enforcement can be added or changed in accordance with the law;
(7) The fine is exempted in accordance with Article 53 of the Criminal Law;
(8) The enforcement respondent is declared bankrupt by a ruling of the people's court;
(9) The subject matter of administrative enforcement is lost;
(10) The case is ordered to be subject to elevated enforcement by a ruling of a higher people's court;
(11) The case is ordered to be enforced by another court by a ruling of a higher people's court;
(12) The procedures for entrustment enforcement have been completed in accordance with the Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on Certain Issues Concerning Entrusted Enforcement, and a notice of case filing from the entrusted court has been received;
(13) Other circumstances that the people's court considers that enforcement should be terminated.

Except for the circumstances specified in items (10), (11), and (12) of the preceding paragraph, if enforcement is terminated, a ruling shall be made and served on the parties.

Article 18 After an enforcement implementation case is filed, under any of the following circumstances, the case may be closed by the method of "case closure":

(1) The enforcement respondent raises a jurisdictional objection, and upon review, the objection is established, and the case is transferred to the court with jurisdiction, or the enforcement applicant withdraws the application;
(2) It is discovered that another people's court with jurisdiction has already filed the case first;
(3) The entrusted court, after reporting to the higher people's court for approval, returns the entrustment.

Article 19 After an enforcement implementation case is filed, if the enforcement respondent raises an application for non-enforcement of an arbitral award or a notarized creditor's document, and upon review, the people's court rules not to enforce, the case shall be closed by the method of "non-enforcement."

Article 20 After an enforcement implementation case is filed, if upon review it is found that it does not meet the acceptance conditions stipulated in Article 18 of the Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on Certain Issues Concerning the Work of People's Courts in Enforcement (for Trial Implementation), and the application is dismissed by ruling, the case shall be closed by the method of "dismissal of application."

Article 21 The methods of closing cases enforcing property preservation rulings include:

(1) Preservation completed, meaning all preservation matters have been fully implemented;
(2) Partial preservation, meaning that due to failure to locate sufficient property, the preservation matters could not be fully implemented;
(3) No subject matter for preservation, meaning no property was found available for preservation.

Article 22 The methods of closing resumed enforcement cases include:

(1) Enforcement completed;
(2) Conclude the current enforcement proceedings;
(3) Termination of enforcement.

Article 23 The following cases shall not be treated as closed:

(1) Cases where the people's court rules to suspend enforcement;
(2) Cases where the people's court decides to temporarily stay enforcement;
(3) Cases where the enforcement settlement agreement has not been fully performed, and the conditions for concluding the current enforcement proceedings or terminating enforcement under Articles 16 or 17 of these Opinions are not met.

Article 24 The methods of closing enforcement objection cases include:

(1) Withdrawal of objection or application allowed, meaning the objector withdraws the objection or application;
(2) Objection or application dismissed, meaning the objection is not established, or the person other than the party has a substantive right over the subject matter of enforcement but cannot prevent enforcement;
(3) Relevant enforcement act revoked, enforcement of the subject matter suspended, enforcement denied, or parties added or changed, meaning the objection is established.

(4) Partial revocation and amendment of the execution act, partial non-enforcement, and partial addition or change of parties, i.e., where the objection is partially sustained;

(5) Inability to revoke or amend the execution act, i.e., where the objection is sustained or partially sustained, but the execution act cannot be revoked or amended;

(6) Transfer of jurisdiction to another people's court, i.e., where the jurisdictional objection is sustained.

A ruling shall be made in execution objection cases and served on the parties. Where laws or judicial interpretations provide that an oral ruling may be made in execution objection cases, it shall be recorded in the transcript.

Article 25: Methods of case closure for execution reconsideration cases include:

(1) Permission to withdraw the application, i.e., where the applicant for reconsideration withdraws the reconsideration application;

(2) Dismissal of the reconsideration application and maintenance of the objection ruling, i.e., where the facts found in the objection ruling are clear, the applicable law is correct, and the reconsideration grounds are not established;

(3) Revocation or amendment of the objection ruling, i.e., where the facts found in the objection ruling are erroneous or the applicable law is incorrect, and the reconsideration grounds are established;

(4) Issuance of a ruling after ascertaining the facts, i.e., where the facts found in the objection ruling are unclear and the evidence is insufficient;

(5) Revocation of the objection ruling and remand for re-examination, i.e., where the objection ruling omits an objection claim or erroneously applies the procedure for examining objections to execution acts to an objection filed by a person not a party to the case.

After a people's court renders a ruling on a re-examined case, if a party applies for reconsideration, the higher people's court may not remand the case for re-examination again.

A ruling shall be made in execution reconsideration cases and served on the parties. Where laws or judicial interpretations provide that an oral ruling may be made in execution reconsideration cases, it shall be recorded in the transcript.

Article 26: Methods of case closure for execution supervision cases include:

(1) Permission to withdraw the application, i.e., where the party withdraws the supervision application;

(2) Dismissal of the application, i.e., where the supervision application is not established;

(3) Order to rectify within a time limit, i.e., where the supervision application is established and the enforcing court is ordered to rectify within a specified time limit;

(4) Revocation and rectification, i.e., where the supervision application is established, the ruling of the enforcing court is revoked and directly rectified;

(5) Elevation of execution level, i.e., where the supervision application is established and the higher people's court decides to elevate the execution level and execute the case itself;

(6) Designation of execution, i.e., where the supervision application is established and the higher people's court decides to designate another court for execution;

(7) Other, i.e., other circumstances where the case may be reported as closed.

Article 27: Methods of case closure for execution request for instructions cases include:

(1) Reply, i.e., where the conditions for requesting instructions are met;

(2) Case closure, i.e., where the conditions for requesting instructions are not met.

Article 28: Methods of case closure for execution coordination cases include:

(1) Withdrawal of the coordination request, i.e., where the courts involved in the execution dispute reach an agreement through consultation and withdraw the coordination request;

(2) Resolution through coordination, i.e., where, after coordination, the courts involved in the execution dispute reach a consensus coordination opinion, and the coordination opinion is recorded in the transcript or a coordination opinion letter is issued to the courts involved in the execution dispute.

Article 29: The filing, execution, and case closure information of execution cases shall be entered into the National Court Execution Case Information Management System in a timely, complete, truthful, and accurate manner.

Article 30: Local people's courts at all levels may not establish standards for case filing and case closure, or methods of case closure, that conflict with laws, judicial interpretations, and the provisions of these Opinions.

Any violation of laws, judicial interpretations, or the provisions of these Opinions in the filing or closure of cases, or any falsification in entering case filing or closure information into the National Court Execution Case Information Management System, shall result in a notice of criticism; if serious consequences or adverse effects are caused, the responsible leaders and personnel shall be held accountable in accordance with the Regulations on Disciplinary Sanctions for People's Court Personnel.

Article 31: Each High People's Court shall actively promote the construction of execution informatization by establishing and improving a case management system that is uniformly used by the three levels of courts within its jurisdiction, practical, fully functional, and scientifically effective, thereby strengthening the management of the filing and closure of execution cases. This includes achieving integrated management of case information on filing, trial, and execution; realizing separate management of cases where the current execution procedure is concluded; achieving dynamic management of cases where execution is resumed; and realizing data linkage between the case management system of its jurisdiction and the National Court Execution Case Information Management System.

Article 32: These Opinions shall come into force on January 1, 2015.
